  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_7b2bb1cfd912469c8fb2a56d088a7a8c",
      "statement": "A job's lifecycle phase is the `status` column on `jobs` (default `pending`). The base vocabulary covers `pending`, `scored`, `filtered`, `ready`, `approved`, `skipped`, `sent`, `replied`, `needs_resume`, `resume_sent`, `follow_up_sent`, `rejected`, and `error`, with two additional runtime statuses: `closed` (written by the sender when the job page is closed/unavailable) and `manual` (shadow jobs created from unmatched HR conversations).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://migrations/postgresql/002_business_data.sql#L1-L8",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1a2681211e1201b2a26e00482b38048baf484ace753fbf2e9695edee600d0af8:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/bosshunter/executor/monitor.py#L1287-L1288",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:9b7257a8063488be72fce7321cd51c58053da82defdffa9d354fa9b7f7867121:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/bosshunter/executor/sender.py#L849-L852",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1188518d6152040fbbb71de1cbe8581dc5a313c8b183bc3e2ac4e0f1cfb961aa:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/bosshunter/tracker/status.py#L15-L45",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:317f5df746de4d7ef90368bff54697a30784563a2b5f53a3e676d968156d2c8f:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_411c2bf0a24e4ae6aaf0898978f19cdf",
      "statement": "Scoring processes only `pending` jobs: a zero quick-score or a deep score below `scoring.threshold` moves the job to `filtered`; a deep score at or above the threshold moves it to `ready` (then batch-generates the greeting); an AI/parse failure leaves it `pending` for retry. Passed `ready` jobs whose greeting ends up empty are rolled back to `approved` so they remain recoverable by regeneration.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/bosshunter/ai/scorer.py#L28-L48",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:360d1d06fe489ac93a8c36ac06ad591d0b538b6234a1416a04dd3e2bb7f8ff37:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/bosshunter/ai/scorer.py#L400-L446",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:975c506c624ccea75bf672dc90345cfbafa7a8a1447b40a9c4ecd0319a923c09:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_cdeaef80a8274a7baea8c169acad2341",
      "statement": "Human confirmation is mandatory before sending and cannot be bypassed by writing the database: `get_jobs_ready_to_send` selects only `approved` jobs with a non-empty greeting, the web `direct_send` endpoint rejects any job that is not already `approved`, and the CLI confirmation prompt defaults to 'n' so empty input never approves a send.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/bosshunter/db.py#L512-L535",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e649668e0936f071c9e4d1033312c2c6c38b563738b07f05a028831eacbc7052:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/bosshunter/ui/confirm.py#L96-L104",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:36692b53feb28f487968aa6516df9502081a0cf6891062c3a31bef8bbe2940d4:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/bosshunter/web/server.py#L1039-L1057",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:068bd119f697ef26d924e8e159e144abfb53c8a3437ea90f5cd52dbd74dc5608:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_1371f7d31ecd4ee5b3f3c6e152489fa5",
      "statement": "Human confirmation moves `ready` to `approved` (confirm), `ready` to `skipped` (skip), and `ready` to `rejected` via the web reject endpoint. The web workbench confirm path marks any non-terminal job `approved` while blocking `rejected`, `closed`, `sent`, `replied`, `resume_sent`, `follow_up_sent`, and `needs_resume`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/bosshunter/ui/confirm.py#L83-L145",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f3d6a29f8b131e3d8923ff0d6b4b208c6cf2acfc0f78fafa321ae4f59743d5ad:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/bosshunter/web/server.py#L990-L1120",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:1b65ac37b0306b8c1130ab96883c5bdd2642f127f8dc9435a634c2e3f0cc681f:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_8a8af9f3b001474c9df6a8711646cf13",
      "statement": "Sending transitions an `approved` job to `sent` on success (writing `history(action='sent')` before the status update for quota accuracy), to `error` on failure (incrementing `error_retry_count`), and to `closed` when the job page is closed or unavailable; an `already_sent` idempotency guard converges the job to `sent` instead of re-sending or failing it.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/bosshunter/executor/sender.py#L822-L872",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:fe654586ba059e35951d7c035ce12400fd2c60fc19eb8cc14e86a32d526af2ac:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f5a38e17fa43429397548c1b1fe7e979",
      "statement": "`recover_send_errors` re-queues `error` jobs whose `error_retry_count` is below the maximum back to `approved` (never `ready`) once a backoff window has elapsed since `updated_at`, preserving the earlier human confirmation; jobs that exhaust the retry count stay `error` until explicitly retried.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/bosshunter/db.py#L414-L451",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:a0d2b5fcb03f63ece2e973f75a92fc0f9faacff9eb0b9413af55ccb0c28491a5:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_55b00c4856bb40a684642d704f772ac0",
      "statement": "Monitoring advances `sent` to `replied` only when the confirmed per-job action is `reply_pending` or `auto_replied` and the prior status is `sent`; HR rejection moves `sent` or `replied` to `rejected`; a successful follow-up moves `sent` to `follow_up_sent`. Shadow `manual` jobs can become `rejected` but do not advance to `replied` because their prior status is not `sent`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/bosshunter/executor/monitor.py#L1340-L1348",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:913f42ca4dbfa389ff24d91c01cb0d1574acb22f105956acabaf2c9a21721165:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/bosshunter/executor/monitor.py#L1592-L1595",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:b1dbfa8ef922329637e128c2d9103156915106e747b968202c314e0468616088:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/bosshunter/executor/monitor.py#L1695-L1709",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3fc79a6bf35462824e0c60a50252795e9e9ebd56e16fc6ee2705a97fb8e7d199:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_bbfc5760a90741c980b698c66c5c9a5c",
      "statement": "Tailored resume generation writes `resume_path` (PDF or Markdown) without changing `status`; `resume_sent` is written by the web `mark-resume-sent` endpoint. `needs_resume` is a defined status mapped to the `resume_requested` event and read by the funnel and monitor, but no current Python write path transitions a job into it.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://migrations/postgresql/003_semantic_layer.sql#L36-L36",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:adb6734e585f15b104784051339b50e3a679894fbd49b35add32be83879f6adf:"
        },
