    {
      "id": "claim_d3460e4d71344102a06c5228bd7ad15f",
      "statement": "`job_events` is the append-only status-transition fact table. A database trigger records `job_collected` on job insert and, on `UPDATE OF status`, maps the new status to an event type (`prefilter_rejected`, `ai_scored`, `greeting_generated`, `user_approved`, `user_rejected`, `greeting_sent`, `hr_replied`, `resume_requested`, `resume_sent`, `follow_up_sent`, `send_failed`, or `status_changed`) with `source = 'database_trigger'`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://migrations/postgresql/003_semantic_layer.sql#L2-L51",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:f31b38713ff331319d3e777ef2c4831306553ac3fbd22a1c28aa0cd81a74d10a:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_0f23cd5ba4394030bc7f26bc8bef9bb8",
      "statement": "The `semantic_job_current` view exposes a one-row-per-job current snapshot (including `ai_score`, `current_status`, and an `is_formal_job` flag), and `semantic_job_funnel` exposes per-job first-arrival times for scored, approved, sent, replied, resume-requested, resume-sent, and follow-up stages computed with `MIN(event_time) FILTER` over the mapped event types.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://migrations/postgresql/003_semantic_layer.sql#L53-L76",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7d8ad3c86f3f38ca00ccc1584d79ad1f94fee19ae1b76e514b627dac454447da:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_84ec1a7b53e347b48c8e5a60c0a36ab1",
      "statement": "The dashboard funnel `get_funnel_stats` derives cumulative stage counts from current status membership (collected, pre-filter passed, AI scored, confirmed, sent, replied, resume-sent, needs-resume, resume-generated, follow-up, rejected), and the CLI status tracker reports reply rate as `replied / sent`.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/bosshunter/db.py#L649-L662",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:307f33e02d2b49acce3c42574b67abe7c0209215f227e3f04ddf0f13a7e285ed:"
        },
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/bosshunter/tracker/status.py#L75-L80",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:7846e238a58ff6a1af2fd72b051cf6cddfe2982445be5036af3048df7edde821:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_0a7b88a090bd448da5b1a2d96d2aeed2",
      "statement": "The assistant semantic layer defines the same funnel deterministically: `SENT_STATUSES` is `sent`, `replied`, `needs_resume`, `resume_sent`, `follow_up_sent`; `REPLIED_STATUSES` is `replied`, `needs_resume`, `resume_sent`, `follow_up_sent`; `reply_rate` is `100 * replied / NULLIF(sent, 0)`; and time-window event metrics count distinct jobs by `job_events.event_type` (`job_collected`, `ai_scored`, `greeting_sent`, `hr_replied`).",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://src/bosshunter/assistant/semantic_layer.py#L69-L108",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e1c6ab1c6c7b473a470099890b81e6afd2b5cc167584ec66d6ef962a42277a4f:"
        }
      ]
    }
